the 11 hours that Haley had with her son  Jack will stay with her forever when he  was born four years ago in Telford the  delivery was traumatic mistakes were  made that cost her son his life when I  heard what happened with Jack and what  it was and someone told me those another  lady the same day and their little lad  got his shoulder stock the same as what  my boy did and they took too long  getting him out and he died the day  before my Jack died and I didn't know  Hayley has long known that there were  many more cases like hers maternity  failings in Telford and Shrewsbury that  have devastated families now a leaked  report has revealed that the inquiry is  dealing with the biggest maternity  scandal the NHS has ever seen in total  270 cases that date back to 1979 it  includes 22 stillbirths 17 deaths of  babies after birth and 51 cases of  cerebral palsy or brain damage medical  failures and failures of human  compassion that created a culture that  was described as toxic that culture goes  back 40 years here in Shropshire the NHS  trust say that they apologise  unreservedly to the families involved  and that big improvements have been made  but even now they have to concede that  their maternity services still have  further to go but nobody can undo the  pain that the families have been through  Richton Rhiannon lost their daughter  Kate shortly after her birth I still  feel angry and I think I didn't have  such a brilliant wife beside me  supporting me it would be a lot  different losing your child losing your  baby watching her die in your arms is a  moment that changes your life forever  I feel bitter hatred quite frankly  towards certain indie  about trust who are enabling overseeing  not caring about baby death maternal  deaths now they know the scale of this  scandal they want corporate manslaughter  charges to follow for now  the inquiry is still working to  establish everything that went so badly  wrong Tom Parmenter Sky News Shropshire
 

